issue.description:
Refine the Studio revenue composition so the chart becomes full-bleed horizontally and extends to the card's bottom edge, while tabs and metrics retain intentional inner padding.

Owner direction:

* Remove the card's current overall outer padding.
* Reapply padding only to the non-chart content blocks.
* Let the chart occupy the full available width of the card and extend all the way to the bottom edge.

Target structure:

Card

* no general outer padding;
* preserve border/radius;
* use overflow clipping if needed so the chart fill respects rounded bottom corners.

Padded top content:

* Week / Month / Quarter tabs;
* Revenue / Margin / Invoices paid metric row.

Full-bleed chart:

* chart reaches the card's left edge;
* chart reaches the card's right edge;
* chart extends to the bottom edge of the card;
* remove chart-side and chart-bottom inset spacing that currently prevents this;
* keep any intentional vertical separation above the chart if visually needed.

Implementation preference:

* Prefer card-level p-0 (or equivalent) with inner wrappers providing spacing for tabs/metrics.
* Keep chart wrapper outside the padded inner content so it can span edge-to-edge.
* Use overflow-hidden or equivalent only if needed to clip the chart cleanly to the card radius.
* Do not fake full-bleed behavior with negative margins if a cleaner structural wrapper change is available.

Preserve:

* current Week / Month / Quarter behavior;
* current Revenue / Margin / Invoices paid metrics;
* current Revenue chart data and interaction;
* current semantic tokens;
* light/dark behavior;
* responsive behavior;
* current card border/radius.

Do not:

* remove padding from the tabs/metrics themselves;
* change the chart data/series;
* change card ordering/layout;
* alter other gallery cards;
* add new tokens or public resources.

Acceptance:

* Studio revenue card no longer relies on one uniform outer padding.
* Tabs and metrics remain comfortably padded.
* Chart spans fully from left to right inside the card.
* Chart reaches the card's bottom edge with no stale bottom inset.
* Chart clips cleanly to the card's rounded bottom corners if applicable.
* No overflow, focus-order, accessibility, responsive, or theme regression.
